  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`{cite}` of `requirements.cli.mdbook` on `struct[Definition]` (`src/lib.rs:121-126`) is the right role.\n\n- **Not a test:** the struct is plain data.\n- **Not an implementation:** it holds three fields (`path`, `text`, `kind`) and makes no decisions, checks, or output. The requirement does not constrain this type's shape. The rendering it requires is done by `preprocess_book`, `replace_references` and `reference_badge`, which carry their own `{impl}` references.\n- **Cite is correct:** `preprocess_book` (`src/lib.rs:176-272`) builds `Definition` values from the book's definition blocks. `DetailPlan` and `render_detail_page` in `src/index.rs` then use them to render requirement definitions and linked badges. If the requirement changed what must be rendered, these fields could need to change, so the struct should stay in sync with it.\n- **Not redundant:** the struct has no `{impl}` or `{test}` reference to the same requirement.",
  "inputs": [
